# F2.6 — the frontend images build from the repo root (a pnpm workspace),
# unlike the backend images, which build from backend/ and have their own
# backend/.dockerignore. Everything below is either dead weight in that
# build context or, for the last two entries, something that must never
# reach an image layer. → CLAUDE.md rule 6

**/node_modules/
**/dist/
.git/

# Local reference material the owner handed over — already excluded from
# git by .gitignore, and 1.4 GB of Cambridge papers/exam packages has no
# business slowing down a frontend image build either.
/Đề IELTS/
/exam/

backend/**/bin/
backend/**/obj/

# User secrets and any environment file. A credential copied into an image
# layer is a credential in every registry that image reaches, and it
# survives being deleted in a later layer.
**/secrets.json
**/secrets.develop.json
**/secrets.production.json
**/.env*
